# What each of the three addresses that are not pages is for.
#
# `robots.txt` names them, `/spec.md`, `/llms.txt` and `/log.xml`, as the three
# the sitemap does not carry, and until the first Search Console report nothing
# answered for them: the feed sat under "crawled, currently not indexed", which
# is where a feed found in every page's <head> stays unless something says so.
#
# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the build output directory, where Astro
# copies site/public/, exactly as it reads _redirects, and serves neither. The
# syntax is a path on its own line and the headers indented under it. The
# reasoning in full is site/README.md § What a machine that is not a browser
# gets; the live check after a publish is under § The domain there.

# A feed is for feed readers, which never look at this header. Declared rather
# than left to the crawler to decide.
/log.xml
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# The same text as /spec/, in the file a model or curl fetches. The header tells
# a search engine which of the two doors to show and changes nothing for anyone
# who fetches the file.
/spec.md
  Link: <https://heroes-lang.org/spec/>; rel="canonical"

# /llms.txt gets nothing on purpose: it has no HTML twin, and noindex would hide
# it from the search crawlers robots.txt says yes to by name.
